Hello,
	I appologize if someone already mentioned this but... I was playing
hack the other day and came across a ghost pile of one of my long dead 
characters.  He was so long dead it surprised me and I thought "someone's been
using my MAC!"  But I realized it was a 6 month old ghost. 
	This brought a thought to mind.  What if there were different kinds of
ghosts?  For instance a recently dead character could be a zombie or skeleton
with hp to reflect the level of the character when he was alive.  And... if
the character has been dead a while the character would be a ghost.  To make
it even more complicated what if the ghost were able to attack you in a manner
that reflected at what level and what class it was in life.  Say a low level
character could not influence the living world with anything more than an 
annoying moan that woke up monsters as you traveled around, a medium level
ghost would moan and throw things at you, and a high level ghost could animate
weapons and attack you.  Also the manner in which you could attack a ghost 
could be different.  For instance a normal sword or weapon should not
be able to harm a ghost.  I think only a blessed weapon or holy water should
be able to affect a ghost or skeleton.  But... say you were to scatter the
bones of a ghost, I think that should do major damage.  So this way a character
would be less inclined to seek out ghosts, if they didn't have holy water or
a blessed item, since at the very least they would be followed around for that
level by a moaning little ghost that woke up all the monsters and at the very
worst a howling spirit that slashed their guts out and with no way to defend
themselves.
	Just a thought...  I sure would like to hear other's thoughts on this.
